# The gateway's replay ring is a convenience, never the truth: a client that never resumes still
# converges. Every reconnect here is a fresh identify with an empty ring, and what bob missed while
# offline comes from the per-group seq cursor he kept and GET /handshakes?from= and
# GET /messages?from=. Nothing he missed is lost and nothing arrives twice.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
group chat kind=text target=d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1d1 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
sync bob
go_offline bob
send alice chat one
send alice chat two
send alice chat three
go_online bob
sync bob
expect_decrypts bob chat one
expect_decrypts bob chat two
expect_decrypts bob chat three
send bob chat back again
expect_decrypts alice chat back again
